# full-only.list — scenarios deliberately kept out of every smoke list.
#
# The smoke (tests/*/smoke.list + smoke-multi.list) is a curated, fast "is this
# build sane" subset: roughly one representative per feature area. Everything
# else stays in the full suite, which is still the release gate. This file is
# what makes that deliberate rather than accidental: scripts/check-test-coverage.py
# fails when a scenario file is neither in a smoke list nor named here, so a new
# scenario can never drift in without a decision (smoke entry, or a reason here).
#
# Format: `# reason: <text>` starts a group; every scenario id below it shares
# that reason until the next `reason:` line. Blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored. An id must name an existing tests/agent/A*.sh or tests/session/S*.sh.
#
# See tests/coverage.map for the feature -> scenario -> smoke map.

# reason: full-suite regression coverage — the curated smoke keeps one
#   representative per feature area for speed; this scenario stays in the
#   release gate.
